David Roth, a realtor and the Democratic nominee for U.S. Senate in [[2022 United States Senate election in Idaho|2022]],<ref>{{Cite web |last1 =Scheufler |first1 =Jordan |last2 =Quinn |first2=Cole|date=June 15, 2025 |title="No Kings" protest in Twin Falls sees hundreds rally at Five Points |url=https://www.kmvt.com/2025/06/14/no-kings-protest-twin-falls-sees-hundreds-rally-five-points/ |access-date=August 26, 2025 |publisher=[[KMVT]] |quote=Speakers at the Twin Falls event included David Roth, who is running for Jim Risch's seat in the U.S. Senate in 2026}}</ref> defeated Nickolas Bonds and Brad Moore<ref name="wr" /> in the May 19 Democratic primary,<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 19, 2026 |title=2026 Idaho U.S. Senate Primary Election Live Results |url=https://apnews.com/projects/elections-2026/idaho-primary-results-us-senate/ |access-date=May 20, 2026 |publisher=Associated Press |language=en}}</ref> but withdrew from the race on July 28.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://idahocapitalsun.com/2026/07/28/idaho-democrat-david-roth-ends-campaign-for-us-senate-seat-held-by-risch/ |title=Idaho Democrat David Roth ends campaign for US Senate seat held by Risch |last=Guido |first=Laura |date=July 28, 2026 |access-date=July 28, 2026 |website=[[States Newsroom|Idaho Capital Sun]]}}</ref>

Matt Loesby, the nominee for Idaho's 1st congressional district in [[2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Idaho#District 1|2024]],<ref>{{cite news |title=Idaho citizens seek elected offices|url=https://www.lmtribune.com/local-news/idaho-citizens-seek-elected-offices-21588153|access-date=March 11, 2026|work=[[The Lewiston Tribune]]|date=February 28, 2026}}</ref> is running as a Libertarian. Former Democratic [[Idaho House of Representatives|state representative]] [[Todd Achilles]]<ref name="AchillesID2">{{cite news |last1=Guido |first1=Laura |title=Idaho lawmaker steps down from Legislature to run for U.S. Senate seat as independent candidate |url=https://idahocapitalsun.com/2025/07/01/idaho-lawmaker-steps-down-from-legislature-to-run-for-us-senate-seat-as-independent-candidate/ |access-date=July 1, 2025 |work=Idaho Capital Sun |date=July 1, 2025}}</ref> and software developer Natalie Fleming<ref name="wr" /> are running as [[Independent politician|independents]].
